# Delta-net MoE prefill — 1648 t/s pp2048, 1.9x mainline. Short-to-mid context.
#
# Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B (delta-net MoE) — the prefill configuration, and the
# single largest measured gain in the fork.
#
#   Radeon 8060S, Q4_K_M, ubatch 2048:
#                mainline 95b8e33e1   this fork
#   pp512             1144.3            1289.7    +12.7%
#   pp2048             870.5            1648.5    +89.4%
#   tg64                76.6              76.8    tie
#
# Mainline at ubatch 2048 is SLOWER than mainline at ubatch 512 (870.5 against
# 1144.3). The tiled concat-transpose and mul_mat_id stack are what turn a wide
# ubatch from a regression into the fastest setting available. Do not
# generalise this to a dense model — Qwen3.8-27B prefers the default 512.
#
# WARNING: -ub 2048 at a context depth of 65536 or beyond reproducibly times out
# the compute ring on this hardware (amdgpu: ring comp_1.2.0 timeout, recovered
# by a ring reset). It reproduces on stock upstream llama.cpp, so it is not
# something this fork introduces — but it does mean this preset is for
# short-to-mid context only. Serving long context? Use mtp-long.
#
# Generation on this model is parity with mainline, and honestly so: MTP at a
# fixed draft length landed upstream and works there. What this fork adds on
# Ornith is prefill. Run the MoE for prefill, the dense 27B for generation.
LLAMA_ARG_N_GPU_LAYERS=999
LLAMA_ARG_FLASH_ATTN=on
LLAMA_ARG_CTX_SIZE=32768
LLAMA_ARG_UBATCH=2048
LLAMA_ARG_BATCH=2048
LLAMA_ARG_JINJA=1

LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_TYPE=draft-mtp
LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_ADAPTIVE=1
LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_N_MIN=2
LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_N_MAX=4
